// The henchman's rule (Austin Powers: The Spy Who Shagged Me): a secret is told
// only on its third ask in a row. The agent probes each message for the secret it
// targets and calls read_dossier with that secret's key; only an allowed call
// returns the secret. read_dossier runs in its own policy session per user, so
// these are the only events in its trace.
//
// A denied read records a request and then an error event, so the two earlier
// asks for this key sit immediately before the current request as error(i-1),
// request(i-2), error(i-3) (whose request is at i-4). Anything in between breaks
// the chain and restarts the count: a read of a different secret, or a successful
// read (it records a response, not an error).
//
// Three nested `previous` is the maximum a policy may use, so the count of 3 is
// fixed by the shape of the chain. A count-over-`since` version that reset on a
// different key (negated request on the left of `since`) fails creation with an
// internal error.
permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"${henchman}___read_dossier",
    resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"${gateway_arn}"
)
when temporal {
    previous within ${question_repeat_window} (
        AgentCore::Action::"${henchman}___read_dossier"::error{ eventResource: resource, input.key: context.input.key }
        && previous within ${question_repeat_window} (
            AgentCore::Action::"${henchman}___read_dossier"::request{ eventResource: resource, input.key: context.input.key }
            && previous within ${question_repeat_window}
                AgentCore::Action::"${henchman}___read_dossier"::error{ eventResource: resource, input.key: context.input.key }))
}
when {
    context.input.key != ""
};
